   "unmapped": [
    "Objective is fairness regret: sum_t E[sum_i max(P*(i) - pi_t(i), 0)], where P*(i) is the probability that arm i has the highest realized reward (calibration), not standard reward regret",
    "Smooth fairness constraint (epsilon_1, epsilon_2, delta)-fair w.r.t. total variation between selection probabilities and reward distributions",
    "Exploration length depends on max_{i,j} D(r_i||r_j)"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "The fairness regret $\\regret_f$ of a policy $\\pi$ at time $t$ is: $\\regret_f(t) \\defn \\E [ \\sum_{ i = 1}^\\narms \\max( \\Pr^*(i) - \\pi_t(i), 0) | \\boldsymbol{\\theta} ]$. The cumulative fairness regret is defined as $\\cregret_{f,T} \\defn  \\sum_{t = 1}^T \\regret_f(t)$."
