    "Objective is fairness regret (deviation from calibrated selection probabilities P(rank(1)=i)), not standard dueling regret",
    "Smooth fairness constraint w.r.t. total variation"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "In a dueling bandit setting, at each time step $t$, the decision maker chooses two arms $a_t(1),a_t(2)$ to ``duel'' with each other. The decision maker doesn't observe the actual rewards ... but rather the outcome $\\mathbbm{1}(r_{a_t(1)}(t) > r_{a_t(2)}(t)).$ ... we adopt the Plackett-Luce (PL) model ... $p_{i,j} = \\frac{\\nu_i}{\\nu_i + \\nu_j}$."
